Generic single-database configuration.

Workflow loop for using alembic to stage and deploy database migrations.
 1. Update python model (change SQLAlchemy models in app/models.py )
 2. Generate an alembic migration
    a. uv run alembic revision --autogenerate -m "add message"
    b. using autogenerate creates a file in backend/alembic/versions/file_with_message.py
    c. review migration in this file that it does what we expect in the def upgrade() fn
    d. common gotcha - nullable=False will cause failures on existing data
3. Apply migration locally
    a. uv run alembic upgrade head
    b. use DBeaver to check migration has applied to the postgres db as expected
4. Commit changes to git
    a. push changes to model AND the alembic version migration
    b. then if someone else pulls this down - they can "uv run alembic upgrade head" to update their local db to current version


uv run alembic history -> shows previous migrations applied
uv run alembic downgrade -1 -> rolls back previous migration